      "contextFingerprint": "02f1b7783b364e6ecf8e6a8c92f0330a7b54594b0a0e190923ff8e28ce8483cc",
      "sourceText": "1. 保存回调时使用默认引用捕获 `[&]`，导致局部变量销毁后仍被访问。\n2. 以为按值捕获会跟着外部变量变化。按值捕获保存的是定义 lambda 时的副本。\n3. 想修改按值捕获的副本，却忘记加 `mutable`。\n4. 把有捕获的 lambda 当成函数指针使用。有捕获的 lambda 需要用模板参数、`auto` 变量或 `std::function` 保存。\n5. 异步场景捕获 `this` 后，对象先被销毁。需要保证对象生命周期，或使用智能指针、`[*this]` 等更明确的方式。",
      "translatedText": "1. Using default reference capture when saving a callback `[&]`, causing local variables to still be accessed after they are destroyed\\.\n2. Assuming that capture by value will change along with the external variable\\. Capture by value stores a copy from when the lambda was defined\\.\n3. Wanting to modify a by\\-value capture copy, but forgetting to add `mutable`\\.\n4. Using a lambda with captures as a function pointer\\. A lambda with captures needs to be saved using a template parameter, a `auto` variable, or `std::function`\\.\n5. After capturing `this` in an asynchronous scenario, the object is destroyed first\\. It is necessary to ensure the object's lifetime, or use a smart pointer, `[*this]` or other clearer approaches\\.",
